Description Task 1: Create a local ssh key directory for the specified user, setting it to mode 0750. This task runs only if the user has manage_ssh_key set to true, and it runs on the localhost without becoming the root user.

Task 2: Manage user {{ user.name }}
Description Task 2: Manage the user creation or modification based on the provided user details including state, password, sudo options, and more.

Task 3: Set sudo options for {{ user.name }}
Description Task 3: Set sudo options for the user by creating a sudoers.d file specific to the user with 0640 permissions and validated using /usr/sbin/visudo --check.

Task 4: Remove sudo options for {{ user.name }}
Description Task 4: Remove the sudo options for the user by deleting the corresponding sudoers.d file if the user does not specify sudo options.

Task 5: Generate private ssh key for {{ user.name }}
Description Task 5: Generate a private ssh key for the specified user if the user has manage_ssh_key set to true. This operation runs on the localhost without becoming the root user.

Task 6: Generate public ssh key for {{ user.name }}
